# Files whose exact bytes are hashed somewhere else. Git must not rewrite them.
#
# Line-ending translation is normally invisible and correct. For these it is
# destructive, and destructive in the worst way: every line stays identical, the diff
# shows nothing, and a recorded sha256 silently stops matching.
#
# Caught twice, both times by a test rather than by review:
#
#   * `predicate-map.csv` — a `git stash -u` round-trip under `core.autocrlf=input`
#     rewrote CRLF to LF. Its digest is recorded in `synthesis-probes.json` as
#     `relation_map_sha256`, which is hashed into `v4-probe-split.json`, so the probe
#     set stopped reproducing from its own seed.
#   * `synthesis-probes.json` — the Windows CI job checks out with `core.autocrlf=true`,
#     which rewrote LF to CRLF and moved the probe-set digest the held-out split names.
#     Linux and macOS passed; only the Windows matrix saw it. That matrix exists for
#     exactly this, and this time it earned its keep.
#   * `configs/beam-eval.json` — a third time, and this one is the rule's own fault. The
#     binding below named `configs/*.yaml`, so a config in a different format was outside
#     it the moment one existed, and `beam-power.json` records that file's digest. The
#     glob is now the directory rather than an extension, so the next config format is
#     covered before it is written rather than after it goes red.
#
# So the rule is stated once over everything that carries a recorded digest, rather than
# per file after each incident. 238 files are bound this way: 122 under `results/`, 85
# under `src/`, 24 under `tools/`, 5 configs, and the two lockfiles — the frozen source
# snapshots and archived conclusions hash them all.
#
# `-text` disables translation in both directions on every platform. It does not mark the
# files binary for diffing; `diff` below keeps them readable in review.

# Evidence: probe sets, archived runs, freezes, manifests, audit records.
results/** -text

# GitHub language statistics should not count machine-produced evidence as product
# source. Markdown protocols and hand-written result reports remain ordinary text; only
# generated data, rows, plots, arrays, and frozen source bundles are marked generated.
results/**/*.json linguist-generated=true
results/**/*.jsonl linguist-generated=true
results/**/*.csv linguist-generated=true
results/**/*.svg linguist-generated=true
results/**/*.npy linguist-generated=true
results/**/source.tar.gz linguist-generated=true
docs/figures/**/*.svg linguist-generated=true
docs/badges/*.svg linguist-generated=true

# Source, tests and configuration. The freeze manifests record a digest per source file
# and `verify` refuses a run whose frozen source no longer matches; `tests/**` is here
# because `release.json`'s `measured_tree_sha256` covers it, and a Windows checkout that
# rewrote the test files would move that digest. Caught by simulating such a checkout
# rather than by another red CI run.
src/**/*.py -text
tests/**/*.py -text
tools/*.py -text
configs/** -text
pyproject.toml -text
uv.lock -text

# Keep them reviewable: `-text` stops translation, not diffing.
*.py diff
*.json diff
*.csv diff
*.md diff
*.yaml diff
